WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.332
RAG failures should be diagnosed by layer.

00:00:03.332 --> 00:00:11.897
If no relevant result appears, inspect the source data, chunking, embedding model, and retrieval method.

00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:19.382
If the right source is retrieved but ranked too low, hybrid retrieval or reranking may help.

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:26.942
If the correct evidence is rank one but the answer still invents a detail, the problem is more likely in prompt design

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:28.412
or generation.

00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:34.384
If an answer is stale, check whether an old document version is still in the index.

00:00:34.384 --> 00:00:37.459
This layered way of thinking saves time.

00:00:37.459 --> 00:00:43.054
Without it, teams often respond to every problem by changing the language model.

00:00:43.054 --> 00:00:49.649
A larger model cannot fix a source that was never indexed, a permission filter that was not applied,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.774
or an outdated vector that was never deleted.

00:00:52.774 --> 00:00:56.796
Debug the system from data to retrieval to generation.
